res: f7 (attacked by queen), g7 (queen), e8 (possibly available?)\n\ne8 is empty — so king can go to e8.\n\nAfter 1. Be8+ Kf8 2. Qg8+ Ke8 — and now what? Queen can’t keep checking easily.\n\nSo not mate.\n\nBut wait — if Black captures the bishop: Kxe8 — then 2. Qg8# — yes! Because:\n\n- King on e8\n- Queen on g8 — attacks g-file and 8th rank\n- King cannot go to d8 (queen on d8), e7 (protected?), f8 (queen), f7 (queen), d7 (no), but:\n  - e8 to f8: attacked by queen\n  - e8 to d8: occupied by Black queen\n  - e8 to e7: attacked by queen? g8 to e7: diagonal? g8-f7-e6 — not e7. No.\n    - g8 to e7: difference of 2 files and 1 rank — not straight line. So not attacked.\n\nSo after Kxe8, Qg8+ — king can go to e7.\n\nNot mate.\n\nWait — is Qg8 even check? Queen on g8, king on e8 — same rank? No, g8 and e8 are same rank (rank 8). Yes!\n\ng8 and e8 are both on 8th rank.\n\nSo queen on g8 attacks entire 8th rank — so yes, Qg8+ checks king on e8.\n\nAfter Kxe8, Qg8+ — then king must leave e8.\n\nAvailable squares: d8 (occupied by own queen), e7, f8.\n\n- d8: blocked\n- f8: attacked by queen\n- e7: not attacked by queen (g8 to e7: not same rank/file/diagonal — no)\n  - So king can go to e7.\n\nSo 1. Bxe8+ Kxe8 2. Qg8+ Ke7 — and Black escapes.\n\nNot mate.\n\nBut what about **Qg8+** first?\n\nQueen on h7 to g8: Q: h7-g8\n\nThat’s a check: Qg8+ — king on e8.\n\nKing must go to d8, e7, f8.\n\n- d8: occupied by Black queen — no\n- e7: possible\n- f8: possible\n\nSo king escapes to e7 or f8.\n\nNo mate.\n\nBut what if we play **Qg8+** and then **Bf7-e8#**?\n\nAfter Qg8+ Kf8, then Be8# — yes!\n\nBecause:\n- 1. Qg8+ Kf8\n- 2. Be8#\n\nCheckmate: king on f8, bishop on e8 — attacks f7, g8, etc.\n- King cannot go to f7 (attacked), g7 (no), g8 (bishop), e8 (bishop), e7 — but is e7 attacked?\n- Bishop on e8 attacks f7, g6, h5 — not e7.\n- Queen on g8 attacks g7, f8, h8, etc.\n\nSo after Be8#, king on f8:\n- f7: attacked by bishop\n- g7: attacked by queen\n- g8: attacked by queen and bish