t\n\nResult: I traded a knight for a rook — net +2 material.\n\nPerfect.\n\nIf I had done nothing, black plays Kxf7 — captures knight, I lose 3, gain nothing — worse by 5 points.\n\nSo Nf7-d8 is urgent and highly profitable.\n\nOther moves delay this and risk losing the knight for nothing.\n\nTherefore, best move is Nf7-d8.\n\nReason: The knight on f7 is under attack by the black king and must be moved or exchanged. Moving it to d8 captures an undefended rook, forcing the black king to recapture, resulting in a favorable exchange of knight for rook (+2 material). Delaying risks losing the knight for no compensation.\n\nAnswer: N: f7-d8'}
