ficient in a position where mate is near.\n- Q: a8-h1 — Long diagonal, but no target; wastes tempo.\n\nThe most forcing and decisive move appears to be **Q: a8-c6**, delivering check and rapidly tightening the net around the black king.\n\nReason: Delivering check with the queen maximizes pressure. Qc6+ forces the black king to b7 (only legal move), after which I can follow up with Rc3-b3+ or Qc6-d5+, potentially leading to mate in a few moves. This is much more effective than slow positional moves.\n\nAnswer: Q: a8-c6"}
