e restrictive.\n- King moves are mostly passive; no need to move the king now.\n- h2-h4 or h2-h3 are slow and irrelevant at this stage.\n\nReason: The most aggressive and positionally dominant move is R: d7-d8, which attacks the 8th rank and directly pressures the black king along the d-file. Since Black’s king is on f6, it cannot easily escape central pressure, and the rook on d8 restricts future movement. This move maximizes activity, controls key squares, and may lead to a quick win by domination or forced mistakes.\n\nAnswer: R: d7-d8'}
