n.\n- K: e3-d3/e3-f3/e3-e4 etc. – King moves may help support d-pawn, but c7 forces the issue more directly.\n\nThe most forcing and winning move is **c6-c7**, as it maximizes progress toward promotion with minimal interference. The black king is too far to stop this pawn without multiple moves, and White can follow up with c8=Q on the next turn unless blocked—there are no black pieces nearby.\n\nReason: Promoting a pawn is the fastest path to victory. Pushing c6-c7 places immediate pressure and creates a near-promotion threat that Black cannot counter in time. It takes full advantage of the position's simplicity and the black king's distance.\n\nAnswer: P: c6-c7"}
