ng will have more difficulty stopping it if supported by my king. Moreover, advancing the b-pawn restricts Black’s king mobility. The alternative P: h4-h5 is slower in terms of coordination and allows Black more time to march the king to the queenside. King moves like K: e3-d4 are tempting for centralization, but immediate pawn advancement increases pressure and limits Black’s responses. Therefore, starting the pawn advance with b4-b5 is most effective.]\n\nAnswer: P: b4-b5"}
