ack’s king and thus has higher winning chances. Advancing it gains tempi.\n\nReason: Pushing the h-pawn with **h5-h6** maximizes winning chances by rapidly advancing a passer away from the enemy king. After h6, I can follow up with h7 and h8=Q, and Black cannot stop it due to distance. The b-pawn is less safe to promote because Black’s king is close to a8.\n\nAnswer: P: h5-h6"}
