; however, with the queen already well-placed, a forcing sequence is better.\n- Q: e7-g7 delivers check and reduces the black king's space immediately — this is a critical move.\n\nReason: The most efficient way to win is to use the queen to restrict the black king’s movement and drive it to the edge. Q: e7-g7 checks the king, forces it to h8, and cuts off the entire g-file. From there, with support from my king if needed, I can follow up with Qh7# or similar. This move makes progress immediately and limits counterplay.\n\nAnswer: Q: e7-g7"}
