: K: f5-g6 places the White king in a strong approaching position, controlling key squares like f7, f8, h7, and h8. This restricts the Black king’s movement and sets up for potential mate-in-two scenarios depending on Black’s reply. It supports the advance toward the corner (h8), where checkmate can be delivered with proper technique.\n\nAnswer: K: f5-g6"}
